        -:  305:/* ============================================================================
        -:  306: * Useless Function Body - if no instruction in the function has an observable
        -:  307: * side effect, NOP the entire body.
        -:  308: * ============================================================================
        -:  309: *
        -:  310: * After all the data-flow folds (const prop, store-load fwd, DCE/DSE) run,
        -:  311: * a function body can be reduced to a forest of LOAD/CMP/JUMPIF chains whose
        -:  312: * eventual consumer (a STORE, CALL, RETURNVALUE, ...) has been killed.  None
        -:  313: * of the surviving ops can be eliminated individually:
        -:  314: *   - LOAD/ASSIGN from a non-volatile sym: still has a "use" via the temp
        -:  315: *   - CMP: uses the temp from the LOAD
        -:  316: *   - JUMPIF: keeps the CMP alive (control op, no temp dest)
        -:  317: * Each link of the chain is alive because the next link reads it, but the
        -:  318: * tail of the chain (the JUMPIF) leads nowhere observable.
        -:  319: *
        -:  320: * If we can prove the *entire function* has no observable side effect, we
        -:  321: * can drop the whole body.  This is the GCC -O2 behavior for things like
        -:  322: * compile/20040304-2.c — a void function whose only "work" is comparing
        -:  323: * cast-folded zeros and conditionally storing into a dead path.
        -:  324: *
        -:  325: * Essential ops (function has observable behavior; skip the pass):
        -:  326: *   - STORE / STORE_INDEXED / STORE_POSTINC, except late-reopt direct writes
        -:  327: *     to non-volatile PARAM vregs after their caller-visible consumers died
        -:  328: *   - FUNCCALLVAL / FUNCCALLVOID unless the callee is a curated pure aeabi helper
        -:  329: *   - FUNCPARAMVAL / FUNCPARAMVOID unless it belongs to such a pure call
        -:  330: *   - RETURNVALUE / TRAP / IJUMP
        -:  331: *   - INLINE_ASM / ASM_INPUT / ASM_OUTPUT
        -:  332: *   - CALLSEQ_BEGIN / CALLARG_REG / CALLARG_STACK / CALLSEQ_END
        -:  333: *   - INIT_CHAIN_SLOT (writes nested-fn chain slot)
        -:  334: *   - PREFETCH (architectural hint — keep conservatively)
        -:  335: *   - SETJMP / LONGJMP / NL_SETJMP / NL_LONGJMP
        -:  336: *   - BUILTIN_APPLY_ARGS / BUILTIN_APPLY / BUILTIN_RETURN
        -:  337: *   - VLA_ALLOC / VLA_SP_SAVE / VLA_SP_RESTORE (stack manipulation)
        -:  338: *   - BLOCK_COPY (memory write)
        -:  339: *   - SWITCH_TABLE / SWITCH_LOAD (jumps + loads)
        -:  340: *   - any LOAD/ASSIGN/CMP/... whose src1/src2 references a sym with VT_VOLATILE
        -:  341: *
        -:  342: * Everything else is "non-essential": pure arithmetic, comparisons, jumps,
        -:  343: * loads from non-volatile memory, etc.  When the entire body is non-essential,
        -:  344: * the function is observationally a no-op and we NOP everything.
